<h1>Business Analytics - Task 2 PPT</h1>
<p>Presenter: <strong>Drisha J</strong></p>

<h2>Overview</h2>
<div class="story">Covers user stories with acceptance criteria, UML diagrams, and API documentation using Postman.</div>

<h2>User Stories</h2>
<details open><summary>1. Registration & Login )</summary><div class="story">Given registration page, when valid info entered, then account created & login works.</div></details>
<details><summary>2. Browse Restaurants </summary><div class="story">Search by location lists nearby restaurants.</div></details>
<details><summary>3. Add to Cart</summary><div class="story">Cart updates quantity/toppings; totals update.</div></details>
<details><summary>4. Secure Payment </summary><div class="story">Successful payment places order.</div></details>
<details><summary>5. Live Tracking </summary><div class="story">Order status updates; notifications sent.</div></details>
<details><summary>6. Ratings & Feedback </summary><div class="story">Delivered orders can be rated; feedback updates restaurant rating.</div></details>
<details><summary>7. Order History )</summary><div class="story">Past orders listed; reorder adds items to cart.</div></details>

<h2>UML Diagrams</h2>
<div class="story"><strong>Activity Diagram:</strong> Login flow, payment success/failure.</div>
<div class="story"><strong>Sequence Diagram:</strong> Customer → System → DB → Restaurant → Payment → Delivery messages.</div>
<div class="story"><strong>Class Diagram:</strong> User, Restaurant, MenuItem, Order, Payment, Delivery; Order hasMany MenuItem.</div>

<h2>API Flow (Postman)</h2>
<div class="box">// Request { POST /v1/order, headers, body } 
// Server { validate → business logic → payment → save order } 
// Response { success 201 {orderId, status, amount} | error 4xx/5xx }</div>

